"diff --git a/docs/ROADMAP.md b/docs/ROADMAP.md\nindex ea5489f6a..ee199aea3 100644\n--- a/docs/ROADMAP.md\n+++ b/docs/ROADMAP.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,15 @@\n # My Roadmap\n \n+- [ ] Under #976 I restore enum identity in the C checker reduce control. My current typechecker unit gate stops at tc_reduce_exact_identities for Choice after scalar, array, record and generic-union cases pass. I retain the failed gate and require the enum-array callback/result contract without weakening the unit assertion.\n+\n+- [ ] Under #976 I diagnose the instrumented interpreter shadow failure for the unchanged 5,000-call generic recursion control. My four-object ASan/UBSan tuple audit passes 39 of 40 methods but the recursive method exits before shadow completion; ordinary C-native and NanoISA runs pass. I retain the failure and require an attributed result before claiming the complete sanitizer suite.\n+\n+- [ ] Under #976 I retain callable values inside interpreter tuples across function return and projection. My expanded native tuple test returns a callback parameter inside nested tuples; parameter cleanup invalidates the retained callback and mandatory shadows report an undefined function. I require owned callable metadata in tuple storage and independent callable projections, with repeated projection, reassignment and sanitizer controls.\n+\n+- [ ] Under #976 I lower qualified imported function values in the self-hosted emitter. My C tuple signature controls now execute pair.flip as a function value, while the qualified self-hosted compiler refuses its declared signature. My expanded generic control also exposes missing qualified callable inference in the self-hosted checker at local and deferred-argument boundaries. I require exact imported owner resolution, local shadowing, contextual generic specialization, signature mismatch refusal and native/VM execution.\n+\n+- [ ] Under #976 I resolve qualified imported function values before ordinary field checking. My tuple-signature audit accept